# The v2 corpus mine's working tree: 2.7 GB of clones, worktrees, checkpoints and
# transplanted samples. Relocated here from benchmark_container on 2026-08-28 so that
# `PROBE_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / "probe_v2"` (scripts/mining/config.py) keeps resolving.
# It must never enter the history this repo split exists to keep small.
# /probe_v2/
.env
probe_v2/history_pairs.jsonl
probe_v2/history_features.jsonl

# Scratch measurement root for the pre-campaign validation pass. It holds one execution per
# role plus its screenshot and `[SPM:err]` log -- a census, not measurements, and its
# buildSpans carry UI-thread printing from `--dump-errors`. `render_gate --apply` merges the
# census into config/render_exclusions.json, which IS committed; this tree is then disposable.
# /dataset-validate/

# Retired measurements. `device_runner discard` MOVES a released group's device dir here
# rather than deleting it, with a `discarded.json` stamp beside it, because the device
# session cost hours and cannot be re-derived. Recovery is `mv`. The tree is not tracked:
# its bytes were tracked until the commit that retired them, so `git checkout <parent> --
# dataset-new_samples/<gid>` recovers them too, and a second 87 MB copy in the history is
# exactly what the repo split exists to avoid.
/dataset-new_samples/_attic/

# Local caches and environments
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
